Changes made in this fork:

  * Rebranded to Sartel; the extension is published as "Sartel".
  * The WebSocket server now verifies the handshake Origin and accepts only
    the Sartel extension (plus one optional development origin), rather than
    accepting any local connection.
  * The extension pins a public key in its manifest so its ID is fixed and
    known ahead of publication.
  * `browser_solve_captcha` was replaced by `browser_captcha_handoff`. The
    CAPTCHA checkbox auto-click, image-grid clicking, and vision-assisted
    solving paths were removed. What remains detects a CAPTCHA and hands it
    to the human.
  * The git-pull self-update on server startup, the extension-copying
    `install` CLI subcommand, and upstream's bundled copy of the extension
    inside the npm package were removed; the extension is distributed through
    the Chrome Web Store.
